{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790460213,"nonce":"ezd52XUbC8fixSaqTseZPn3gF0s=","message":"Design settled with the user (2026-09-26): each runtime keeps its own compiled (erased) types, and the boundary casts. The AOT takes a link table from the host: (lib, native name) -\u003e the callee symbol, the callee's machine signature, a cast function for each argument that needs one (by name; none for a scalar that is the same machine type), and one for the result. For such a native, natives.rs emits: cast each argument, call the symbol, cast the result. Ash never names caribou; it calls the functions the table names. No rt seam slots are needed. Untyped natives get no entry.","files":null}]}